<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20270" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hăruspĭcīnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ar-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>relating to the inspection of
				victims.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quod Etruscorum declarant et haruspicini et
					fulgurales et tonitruales libri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 33, 72</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hăruspĭ-cīna</span></b> ,
			ae, f. (sc. ars), <i>the art
				of divining</i>, <i>divination</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratio, quae haruspicinae disciplina
					continetur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 23, 50</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Fam. 6, 18, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
